Commands to verify server and platform administrative ownership, manage
cryptographic root signing secrets, and check ownership vault status.

Usage:
  orbit admin [command]

Available Commands:
  grant         Generate an 8-digit single-use authorization code for a new admin
  init          Initialize and verify platform server ownership via email OTP challenge
  rotate-secret Rotate root master signing secret in the sealed owner vault
  status        Display platform ownership verification status, vault integrity, and mail config
  totp          Manage two-factor authentication and user TOTP recovery
  verify        Seal owner.json locally (hermetic OTP; no API call)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for admin

Global Flags:
      --config string   Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file

Use "orbit admin [command] --help" for more information about a command.
